      neutralCase: "The current market reflects a cautious yet undeniable progression towards TradFi-DeFi integration. While institutional interest is growing and tokenization presents clear advantages, the path forward is complex, fraught with regulatory hurdles and market inefficiencies. The speculative elements, while innovative, introduce volatility that may deter more conservative investors, suggesting a gradual, rather than explosive, convergence.",
      probabilityWeightedOutlook: "There is a high probability (70%) of continued, albeit uneven, integration between traditional finance and crypto. Institutional adoption will likely expand, focusing on regulated products and proven blockchain applications. Tokenization will grow steadily, contingent on regulatory clarity. However, the probability of significant volatility and liquidation events in highly speculative crypto-native derivatives remains medium (50%), especially around traditional market events. The overall long-term outlook for a hybrid financial system is strong, but short-to-medium term challenges persist.",
